KEY (indirect height bound): for a SINGLE cluster, the difference-core scale = the
INTERNAL SPREAD (range of k_r), NOT the height (13*min k_r). mac-mini decorrelation:
safe(cluster) ~ safe(diffcore) at the carrier. So height is IRRELEVANT to safe -- only
the bounded internal structure matters => the height-INFINITE direction collapses to a
FINITE diffcore check. The AP (all k_r equal => diffcore={1..11}) is the fixed point.

